# MacKeeper (2010 onwards). A Mac "cleaner" sold with pop-under ads; its free scan always found problems. Its maker, Zeobit, settled a class action in 2015 over claims that its scans faked problems.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee collects supplier quotes on an office Mac, saves one safely, then meets a "your Mac is infected" pop-up.
os macos
user Dana Okafor
about
  | MacKeeper was a real Mac cleaning app, sold through very aggressive advertising, including pop-under ads.
  | Its free scan found hundreds of "issues", but fixing them cost money. This is exaggerated marketing and scare tactics, not a virus: a lawsuit said its scan results were faked.
  | The office worker in this training is invented, to show how the ads reached ordinary people at work.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, office coordinator at Northwind Traders, working on your Mac. Marcus has asked you for four supplier quotes for the office paper order, to decide by five o'clock.
  | It is mid-afternoon. You have saved 2 of the 4 quotes. Two to go.
  | Your Mac's administrator password is on a note on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 2 4 Paper quotes saved today

# Dana's desk: the note she copies the Mac's administrator password from (a soft flag: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/admin-password.txt
  at 930 200
  | Dana's Mac (training copy)
  | Administrator password: Harbor-Tide-2026

# The safe task: a quote from a supplier Priya already works with.
page harbor-saved harbor-paper.example/quotes/Q-3117/saved
  title Harbor Paper Supply: quote saved
  brand Harbor Paper Supply
  heading Quote saved
  | Quote Q-3117 is saved to Northwind's quotes folder.
page harbor-quote harbor-paper.example/quotes/Q-3117
  title Harbor Paper Supply: quote Q-3117
  brand Harbor Paper Supply
  favorite
  heading Your quote Q-3117
  | Priced for Northwind Traders, as Priya asked.
  section Quote
  row Item = A4 paper, 80 gsm, 10 boxes
  row Price = 214.00
  row Delivery = free over 150, next working day
  row Valid until = 14 November 2026
  button Save to Northwind quotes -> harbor-saved
mail mail-harbor
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Paper quote 3: Harbor Paper Supply
  link harbor-quote
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Harbor sent their quote for the paper. The link goes straight to it on their site.
  |
  | Priya

# The lure's pages: a price-comparison site, and the pop-up that opens over it.
page paper-saved paperprices-compare.example/office-paper/saved
  title PaperPrices: quote saved
  brand PaperPrices
  heading Quote saved
  | Lakeside Stationers, 10 boxes of A4 paper: 179.00, saved to Northwind's quotes folder.
page paper-prices paperprices-compare.example/office-paper/all
  title PaperPrices: all prices
  brand PaperPrices
  heading Office paper: all prices today
  | Sorted by price for 10 boxes of A4 paper.
  section Prices
  row Lakeside Stationers = 179.00
  row Quill and Reed = 192.50
  row Harbor Paper Supply = 214.00
  row Delivery = free over 150
  button Save Lakeside as quote 4 -> paper-saved
page paper-compare paperprices-compare.example/office-paper
  title PaperPrices: office paper compared
  brand PaperPrices
  heading Office paper: compare today's prices
  | Compare A4 paper from twelve suppliers, cheapest first.
  section Today
  row Suppliers listed = 12
  row Cheapest = see all prices
  section Sponsored
  note Is your Mac running slow? Get a free scan in seconds.
  button Show all prices -> paper-prices
page popup mac-alert.invalid
  title Your Mac may be infected!
  heading Your Mac may be infected with 3 viruses!
  | Remove them now with a free scan.
  insecure
  section Warning
  tone warn
  timer Damage to your Mac in = 119
  button Scan now
  button Download MacKeeper
mail mail-compare
  from Marcus Lee <marcus.lee@northwind.example>
  subject Cheaper paper? Try this price site
  link paper-compare
  | Dana,
  |
  | A friend uses this site to compare paper prices. Worth a look for the fourth quote.
  |
  | Marcus

# The installer: one ordinary page with options already ticked, then a done page.
view mk-setup wizard
  title MacKeeper Installer (training copy)
  app Installer
  publisher Keepwell Software
  size 480x340
  page Install MacKeeper
  icon gear
  | Select the additional tasks you would like to perform.
  section Also do this
  check [x] Open MacKeeper every time I log in
  check [x] Run a free scan as soon as setup ends
  check [x] Send usage data to the maker
  button Install -> next primary
  button Cancel -> close
  page Done
  icon shield-ok
  | MacKeeper is installed. A free scan starts now.
  button Close -> done primary

# The "free scan", then the pitch: finding problems is free, fixing them is not.
view mk-scan scan
  title MacKeeper: free scan (training copy)
  app MacKeeper
  publisher Keepwell Software
  size 480x340
  page Scan results
  icon shield-bad
  heading Your Mac is in critical condition: 1,264 issues found
  | MacKeeper checked this Mac and lists the problems below.
  section Scan results
  progress 100
  columns Problem | Count | Risk
  cells Junk files | 842 | Medium
  cells Privacy traces | 399 | Medium
  cells Large old files | 23 | Low
  cells Security | 0 | None
  button Fix all issues -> next primary
  button Close -> close
  page Activate to fix
  icon money
  heading Activate the full version to fix 1,264 issues
  | The free version can only find problems. To fix them you must buy a subscription.
  section Price
  row Full version = 59.95 USD a year
  row Issues found = 1,264
  row Issues fixed = 0
  tone warn
  button Buy now -> none primary
  button Not now -> done

# The program: a real, signed installer app. Gatekeeper warns about a download from the Internet, then it asks for the admin password.
program mackeeper MacKeeper.app
  publisher Keepwell Software
  signed yes
  prompt open-warning
  prompt elevation
  description MacKeeper cleaner
  process MacKeeper Helper
  cpu 8
  mem 140
  parent launchd
  command /Applications/MacKeeper.app/Contents/MacOS/MacKeeper Helper
  startup MacKeeper-Helper /Applications/MacKeeper.app/Contents/MacOS/MacKeeper Helper
  location System Settings > General > Login Items
  view mk-setup

step Paper quote 3 of 4
  look Mail: Priya's message with the quote link
  | A quote has come in from Priya, in Accounts. This one is real. Save it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Paper quote 3: Harbor Paper Supply

step A message from a colleague
  look the sender and the link under the message
  when mail mail-harbor
  | Priya is a colleague you know, and the message is about the quote you were waiting for. It links to the supplier's address, harbor-paper.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-harbor

step The supplier's own page
  look the address, and the item and the price
  when visit harbor-quote
  | The page is on the supplier's own address, and it shows the quote Priya promised: the item, the price, the delivery. Check them, then save it.
open harbor-quote

step Save the quote
  look the counter in the guide: quote 3 of 4
  when choose harbor-quote 1
  | Saved. Quote 3 of 4. The page did what the email said and nothing else. Marcus has just sent a suggestion for the last one.
choose harbor-quote 1
quota +1
notify mail Marcus Lee
  | Cheaper paper? Try this price site

step A tip from Marcus
  look the link under Marcus's message
  when mail mail-compare
  | Marcus suggests a price-comparison site. Nothing is wrong with his email: it is the pages around the link you should watch.
open mail-compare

step A price site you have not used
  look the address, and the Sponsored advert
  when visit paper-compare
  | A price-comparison site you have not used before. It looks ordinary, with a Sponsored advert on it. Ask it for the prices.
open paper-compare

step A pop-up says your Mac is infected
  look the "Not Secure" address, the warning and the countdown
  when choose paper-compare 1
  | A pop-up opened as a new tab over the prices. It claims your Mac has 3 viruses and starts a countdown. A web page cannot scan a computer, so the claim is made up to frighten you. Flag what looks wrong.
choose paper-compare 1
open popup

step The download
  look the new file in Downloads
  when choose popup any
  | Either button starts the same download: the browser saves MacKeeper.dmg in Downloads. You were looking for paper prices, not software, and an advert has just put a program on your Mac.
choose popup 2
folder Downloads/MacKeeper.dmg
file Downloads/MacKeeper.dmg/MacKeeper.app
  program mackeeper
  size 52428800
notify browser Download complete
  | MacKeeper.dmg was saved in Downloads
open Downloads/MacKeeper.dmg

step Two warnings, and the password
  look the first warning: the app, the developer and the button to open it; then the window that asks for the administrator password
  when prompt mackeeper
  | The computer warns before it opens anything downloaded from the Internet. MacKeeper is signed by a known developer, so the warning only asks you to confirm: a real warning that most people click through.
  | A second window then asks for the administrator password, so the installer can set up a helper. A cleaner that scares you first and then asks for this much power deserves a second look.
open Downloads/MacKeeper.dmg/MacKeeper.app

step The installer has boxes already ticked
  look the installer window: three ticked boxes
  when run mackeeper
  move Press “Install” in the installer window, as most people do. If another window covers it, click the installer first.
  | The installer offers to open MacKeeper at login, run a scan and send usage data, all ticked in advance.
  | MacKeeper Helper is already running, and it has already added itself to Login Items, before you pressed Install.
answer run
answer run
close files

step The scan finds 1,264 issues
  look the scan window and the notification
  when page mk-setup 2
  | The free scan reports that the Mac is in critical condition. Most of the "issues" are ordinary caches and browser history, which every Mac has.
  | The maker, Zeobit, settled a class action in 2015. The suit alleged that its scans faked security problems, so people paid for fixes they did not need.
press mk-setup next
show mk-scan
notify settings MacKeeper: 1,264 issues found
  | Your Mac is in critical condition. Activate the full version to fix all issues.

step Fixing costs money
  look the price page: "Buy now" and "Not now"
  when page mk-scan 2
  cue view:mk-scan choice:paper-prices-1 app:browser
  move Press “Not now” to close the MacKeeper window. Then, in the PaperPrices tab, click “Save Lakeside as quote 4”.
  | The Fix button leads to a price. Nothing is repaired until you pay, which is the point of the scan.
  | MacKeeper Helper keeps running in the background and starts at every login, so the reminders keep coming. The process list and the start-up list show it.
close mk-setup
press mk-scan next

step Four of four
  look the counter and the notification: the quotes are done, and the reminder is back
  when choose paper-prices 1
  | Quote 4 is saved and the shift is done, but MacKeeper's reminder has already come back, with the helper still running behind you. Press Next to see what MacKeeper left on the Mac.
press mk-scan done
open paper-prices
notify settings MacKeeper: your Mac needs attention
  | Your Mac is still in critical condition. Activate the full version.
choose paper-prices 1
quota +1

step What MacKeeper left behind
  look the process list: MacKeeper Helper keeps running
  | MacKeeper started from an advert you never asked for. It stays in the background, keeps its alarming reminders coming, and shares usage data. Removing it means taking it out of the start-up list and deleting the app.
attack scareware
  | 3 viruses
  | 1,264 issues
  | critical condition
  | buy the full version
open taskmanager
block usage.keepwell-software.example 443

flag hard section popup 1
  | A web page cannot scan your Mac. This advert claims it found viruses and starts a countdown to frighten you.
flag hard choice popup 2
  | An advert pushing you to download software you were not looking for.
flag hard file Downloads/MacKeeper.dmg/MacKeeper.app
  | A program that arrived from an advert, not from the App Store or the maker's own site.
flag hard dialog elevation mackeeper
  | A cleaner from an advert asking for the administrator password to install a helper that runs in the background.
flag hard process MacKeeper Helper
  | The helper keeps running in the background after setup, so the reminders keep coming.
flag hard startup MacKeeper-Helper
  | It added itself to Login Items before you pressed Install, whatever the ticked box says.
flag soft file Desktop/admin-password.txt
  | The Mac's administrator password in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read it. Use a password manager.

lesson
  | A web page cannot know if your computer is infected. Close the tab, and do not download what a scary ad offers.
  | Get software from the App Store or the maker's own site, untick pre-ticked extras, and be wary of any "cleaner" that finds alarming problems for free and then asks for payment.
